                                                                  1021 1451
  Temperatures = 293.6 400 500 600 700 800 1000 1200 1600 2000 K  1021 1451
                                                                  1021 1451
 HISTORY                                                          1021 1451
 -------                                                          1021 1451
 This evaluation was generated by Naval Nuclear Laboratory [1]    1021 1451
 using FLASSH [2].  The physical model is based on a generalized  1021 1451
 elastic scattering treatment and includes coherent elastic       1021 1451
 scattering and inelastic scattering components at 10             1021 1451
 temperatures.  The evaluation is intended to be used with the    1021 1451
 companion Be(Be2C) TSL evaluation when modeling beryllium        1021 1451
 carbide.                                                         1021 1451
                                                                  1021 1451
 THEORY                                                           1021 1451
 ------                                                           1021 1451
 Beryllium carbide (Be2C) has a cubic anti-fluorite (CaF2)        1021 1451
 crystallographic structure (Fm3m space group) with four          1021 1451
 molecules per unit cell [3].  The coherent elastic scattering    1021 1451
 cross sections were evaluated in the cubic approximation using   1021 1451
 the FLASSH generalized elastic scattering treatment based on     1021 1451
 the Be2C unit cell crystal structure [3], the measured room      1021 1451
 temperate unit cell lattice parameter of 4.3420 Ang from [4]     1021 1451
 and the Be and C free atom scattering cross sections from        1021 1451
 ENDF/B-VIII.0.  The inelastic scattering cross sections were     1021 1451
 evaluated in the incoherent approximation using the Be and C     1021 1451
 phonon density of states from a first-principles VASP/PHONON     1021 1451
 calculation [1] using a 3x3x3 supercell, a phonon order of 400,  1021 1451
 and LO/TO splitting to better capture the higher energy          1021 1451
 vibrational modes.                                               1021 1451
